  "notes": "Pickled tensors (DTI and GIS vehicle groups) without channel names or units; Labels.xls labels the DTI folders. The landing page states the release covers 515 vehicles and three battery models, of which 121 folders are present. Charging profile: null: the registry says MultiC, but the DTI/GIS files are unlabelled tensors with no readable current channel and the source states no charge current, so the charge rates could not be checked. Unresolved. The paper and the Zenodo record state that the vehicles come from three battery manufacturers, anonymised as DTI, QAS and GIS; the cell type, chemistry and capacity of each are not given, so the cell fields stay null. Paper (read in full): 18.2 million valid entries from 515 vehicles in the Beihang BMS cloud, from three battery manufacturers anonymised as DTI, QAS and GIS \"due to confidentiality restrictions\"; inputs are voltage, temperature, current, on-board SOC, speed and mileage, with sampling intervals of 30 s at most; fault labels (thermal runaway, electrolyte leakage, internal short circuit, excessive aging) were assigned by engineers after pack disassembly. The paper names no cell type, chemistry, capacity or pack configuration, so the cell fields stay null; this was checked against the full text, not only the abstract."
